# Wrangler's generated binding + runtime types. Committed on purpose: CI runs
# `wrangler types --check`, which fails when the checked-in file no longer
# matches the config, so a new Durable Object binding cannot ship without its
# types. That check is the reason these are not simply ignored.
#
# The cost is that ~14.7k of those lines are workerd's own API surface, so
# every wrangler upgrade rewrites the whole file. Marking them generated keeps
# that out of review: GitHub collapses the diff, and `-diff` stops git
# producing a textual one at all.
worker-configuration.d.ts linguist-generated=true -diff
worker-configuration.preview.d.ts linguist-generated=true -diff
